[2026-06-26 13:02] ⚙️ BACKEND: === BACKEND ENGINEERING STARTED ===
[2026-06-26 13:02] BACKEND: Architecture: CRDT-based event system with multi-tenant isolation

[2026-06-26 13:02] BACKEND: === EVENT MODEL DESIGN ===
  Event Types:
    - BLOCK_INSERT: { blockId, position, type, content, userId, hlc }
    - BLOCK_UPDATE: { blockId, content, version, userId, hlc }
    - BLOCK_DELETE: { blockId, userId, hlc }
    - BLOCK_MOVE: { blockId, newPosition, userId, hlc }
    - WORKSPACE_JOIN: { userId, role }
    - WORKSPACE_LEAVE: { userId }

  Event Queue:
    - In-memory queue per workspace
    - Events are CRDT operations (commutative)
    - No ordering required (CRDT property)

[2026-06-26 13:02] BACKEND: === SYNC STRATEGY ===
  Pull-based (simulated real-time):
    - GET /api/workspaces/{id}/sync?since={hlc}
    - Returns events since given HLC
    - Client merges events into local state

  Push:
    - POST /api/workspaces/{id}/events
    - Array of CRDT operations
    - Server applies to in-memory state
    - Returns updated HLC watermark

  Offline:
    - Queue events locally
    - Push on reconnect
    - CRDT guarantees correct merge

[2026-06-26 13:02] BACKEND: === CONFLICT LOGIC (CRDT) ===
  Block Update Conflict:
    - Два пользователя редактируют один блок
    - LWW-Register: per-character last-write-wins
    - HLC определяет "last"
    - No data loss (characters may interleave)

  Position Conflict:
    - Два пользователя вставляют блок в одну позицию
    - Fractional index: insert between
    - Оба блока существуют, порядок определён дробным индексом

  Delete-Update Conflict:
    - User A удаляет блок, User B обновляет
    - Delete wins (tombstone)
    - Update игнорируется для tomstoned block

[2026-06-26 13:02] BACKEND: === MULTI-TENANT ISOLATION ===
  Data isolation:
    - Every query scoped by workspaceId
    - No cross-workspace access in data layer
    - Tenant ID in all event headers

  Permission check:
    - Every API call validates user role in workspace
    - viewer: read only
    - editor: read + write
    - owner: read + write + manage users

  Attempt simulation:
    - Tenant A user tries to access Tenant B workspace → 403
    - Viewer tries to edit → 403
    - Escalation attempt → logged, rejected

[2026-06-26 13:02] BACKEND: === API ENDPOINTS ===
  POST   /api/workspaces                    → create workspace
  GET    /api/workspaces/{id}               → get workspace
  POST   /api/workspaces/{id}/events        → push events
  GET    /api/workspaces/{id}/sync          → pull events
  POST   /api/workspaces/{id}/users         → add user
  PUT    /api/workspaces/{id}/users/{uid}   → change role
  GET    /api/workspaces/{id}/blocks        → get all blocks
  POST   /api/workspaces/{id}/blocks        → insert block
